{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790993606,"nonce":"JyPUTXQn62f0csGgKte0qNIpxRQ=","message":"Input events landed in 3477ac2.\n\nDone:\n- blinc_abi/src/hit.rs hit-tests the way the paint walk draws: through transforms, inside clips, last child on top.\n- ashui.input.Pointer dispatches enter and leave (not bubbling), plus move, down, up, click and wheel, which bubble from the topmost node with local coordinates. A click goes to the deepest node both the press and the release were over.\n- Keyboard routes hlwindow KeyEvents and text (typed or IME commit) to the focused node, bubbling. Tab and Shift+Tab move focus; Enter, and Space on release, click.\n- Events use hlwindow's own Key, MouseButton and Modifiers types. hxx takes onClick, onPointerDown/Up/Move/Enter/Leave, onWheel, onKeyDown/Up, onTextInput, onFocus and onBlur. WindowedApp forwards all of them; wheel lines are 40 layout units, as in Blinc.\n\nStill to do here: a text field (caret, selection, editing, IME preedit), scroll containers that consume wheel events, and drag.\n\nKnown: under Ash hybrid mode signals stop taking writes partway through the smoke run (Ash 6208fb0, reproducer tests/fixtures/ash/hybrid_signal); interp and jit pass everything.","files":null}]}